{
  "description": "Session 44 and older hash rules, the specific color rules (config.rules: qual, val) and Feature visibility rules (features.featureVisibilityManualRules: qualifier, value), with the Session's diagram mode, its saved feature catalog (projected to the fields the readers use), and its request records, and the rules both readers must produce. Such a Session matched hash= against the drawn feature; hash= names the source hash now (release D-39). A value, written <hash> or ^<hash>$ and maybe with the rendered ID's record and instance suffixes (release 0.13.0), names the catalog features drawn with that hash (drawnSelector.hash, or the svgId hash before catalog schema 5), in the record its suffix gives; when they share one source hash, the value names it in the same form without the suffixes. Every other hash value is kept, and counted in unmappedCount when a request record is drawn cropped, reverse-complemented, or rotated. A list without a change is returned as saved. Read by tests/test_session_compat.py (session_io.migrate_session_hash_rules) and tests/web/feature-edit-migration.test.mjs (migrateSessionHashRules).",
